From: iamwrm <iamwrm@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 19:59:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 05/16] feat(fork): add HERDR_REMOTE_TIMING for remote attach
 phase diagnostics

Set HERDR_REMOTE_TIMING=1 to print per-phase timing to stderr during
`herdr --remote` setup: config load, every ssh round-trip (labelled with
the remote command), the prepare/server-ready phases, total setup time,
and the bridge ssh transport spawn.

Windows has no ssh ControlMaster, so the launcher's five discovery and
status round-trips are each a fresh TCP+KEX+auth connection; on slow or
high-latency links they dominate attach time. The timing output shows
whether the cost is per-connection (network/auth - fix with ssh-agent,
GSSAPIAuthentication=no, AddressFamily inet, or a faster KexAlgorithm)
or a slow remote command (server status, version probe).
